# The free fast path's route byte: each wrapper is one core atomic
# operation (or AtomicU8::new), and `fixed` is kept because fetch_or of
# bits within ROUTE is the only write after `new`.
new	atomics primitive	loom/GenMC	trusted (partly checked, Kani: kani_proofs::atomic::flags_route_byte; not checked: concurrent interleavings, where the orderings matter; that every write after `new` is `fetch_or` within `ROUTE` (the harness makes no other); that `fixed` is kept when the byte is moved into place (`put_flags`' `ptr::write`))
load	atomics primitive	loom/GenMC	trusted (partly checked, Kani: kani_proofs::atomic::flags_route_byte; not checked: concurrent interleavings, where the orderings matter; that every write after `new` is `fetch_or` within `ROUTE` (the harness makes no other); that `fixed` is kept when the byte is moved into place (`put_flags`' `ptr::write`))
fetch_or	atomics primitive	loom/GenMC	trusted (partly checked, Kani: kani_proofs::atomic::flags_route_byte; not checked: concurrent interleavings, where the orderings matter; that every write after `new` is `fetch_or` within `ROUTE` (the harness makes no other); that `fixed` is kept when the byte is moved into place (`put_flags`' `ptr::write`))
